# Napier 8 hp open two-seater, 1900-1903.
#
# The first Napier production car, built at Lambeth: a double phaeton with two
# rows of seats, a sloping perforated nose and no windscreen. AP 3575 is one of
# the three original cars. Napier production reached 250 cars in 1903 and 743
# in 1913. The single-row two-seater body is not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napier_%26_Son
#
# Dimensions 3.5 x 1.65 x 1.55 m, wheelbase 2.153 m. Length and width are
# estimates measured from the photographs; the wheelbase is published.
#
# Shape reference: a true level side photograph of AP 3575, plus front
# three-quarter and detail views of the same car. No rear three-quarter of
# AP 3575 exists in Commons, so the tail follows the side view. Recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d), no period UK document consulted. Black, Dark Green,
# Maroon and Grey are plain colour names, the common finishes of the period.
# Weights 2, 1, 1, 1, total 5, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 50 km/h. Comfort 18/357, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 18. Class 4.
# Dates 1900-1903 production, road tail staggered 1912-1914.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/napier-8.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/napier-8.dae. References: citycars/references/napier-8/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: AP 3575 is modelled as the double phaeton with two seat
# rows, the sloping perforated nose and no windscreen; the single-row two-seater
# body is not represented. The true side governs; no rear view exists, so the
# tail follows the side and the elevated detail photograph. Segmented curves,
# turned-up mudguard ends and seat scallops are simplified.


obj=citycar
